  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing Initial Skills**\n\nI\'m assessing the available skills, specifically \"cloudsql-setup\" and \"cloudsql-update\", in relation to the **SonicObsidian** application requirements. I need to determine their relevance to the application\'s design, style, and mockups. I\'m focusing on how these skills can be leveraged in the initial setup and potential updates of the application.\n\n\n**Evaluating Skill Suitability**\n\nI\'m now evaluating the relevance of various skills. The user\'s requirements seem to align with \"image-generation\" for high-fidelity album art. Additionally, \"focus-mode,\" while potentially relevant for UI interactions, seems less critical given the nature of the application. I\'m prioritizing \"image-generation\" due to the user\'s specific mention of images in the HTML. I can leverage hotlinked images as described in the prompt.\n\n\n**Extracting Image URLs**\n\nI\'m now going through the HTML mockups to extract the image URLs that are already present. My aim is to identify all hotlinked images directly mentioned in the user\'s prompt. Then, I\'ll identify if the user requires features powered by Gemini AI. I\'m also considering the user\'s mention of real-time data visualization; it seems I can use `recharts` or `d3` for this. I\'m evaluating the necessity of incorporating a smart AI assistant or other AI recommendations.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Exact Specifications**\n\nI\'ve just revisited the project goals and, crucially, I see the emphasis on avoiding unsolicited features, and delivering the specified scope precisely. I\'m focusing on the provided screenshots and HTML, and will now limit my focus to the elements present. My immediate task is to identify and implement only the components explicitly described by the user, and nothing more. I will ensure that any feature not specifically requested is excluded, to avoid a critical failure.\n\n\n**Visualizing Application Screens**\n\nI\'m now visualizing the application screens. I\'ve broken down the design into four distinct screens, and I\'m cataloging elements for each: the player bar, the now-playing full-screen view with album art and lyrics, the user\'s library with playlists, and a playlist details screen. I\'m focusing on ensuring these mockups are meticulously recreated. I\'ll maintain fidelity to the described layouts, and each view\'s components.\n\n\n**Implementing Interactive Elements**\n\nI\'m now fully focused on implementing the interactive components. I\'m prioritizing the real-time audio visualizers and data visualizations. I\'m exploring integration with `recharts` for the analytics dashboard, and ensuring the UI is responsive, and toggles between light and dark modes effectively. The player bar, simulated playback progress, and lyrics highlighting will be fully functional, and working in real-time. I\'m planning to make an \"Audio Visualizer & Audio Analytics Dashboard\" tab.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I am going to check the `package.json` and other configuration files to understand the pre-installed libraries and workspace configuration."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 157867557
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
