    thinking: "**Analyzing Screen Breakdown**\n\nI\'m now diving into splitting the application\'s structure. My focus is on effectively modeling the user\'s desired screens, starting with a breakdown of Screen 1: the Home dashboard. I\'m aiming for a clear separation of concerns in the application architecture, anticipating the need for multiple views matching the provided screenshots.\n\n\n**Expanding Screen Set**\n\nI\'ve expanded the screen set! I\'ve visualized the Your Library tab as a clean playlist list, plus liked songs and followed artists. The \"My Masterpiece\" Playlist Detail view is taking shape, and the full-screen \"Now Playing\" interface is detailed with lyrics, controls, and a visualizer. Notably, I\'ve added a **\"Real-Time App/Audio Analytics Dashboard\"** with streaming habits and genre breakdowns.\n\n\n**Defining Data Types**\n\nI\'m now concretizing data structures. I\'m focusing on defining core types like `Song`, `Playlist`, and `Artist` within `/src/types.ts`. I have specified fields for each type, incorporating both basic information and details for richer features. The `Song` type includes fields like `lyrics` and `genre`, while `Playlist` covers details like `description`, `covers`, and `isPublic`. I\'m using `durationSec` instead of `duration` for performance. The `Artist` type includes `tracksCount` and `type`.\n\n\n**Extracting Design Assets**\n\nI\'m now focused on the visual fidelity. I\'ve extracted image URLs like a jazz musician and neon turntable, ensuring pixel-perfect replication of the screenshots. These URLs are now categorized by their design purpose. I\'m prioritizing accuracy in replicating the original design assets.\n\n\n**Gathering Visuals**\n\nI\'m now collating the visual assets. I\'ve successfully extracted the required image URLs, specifically a mic and spotlight, an aurora landscape, and a grand piano. I\'m making sure these are the best quality for the design. They\'ll be categorized by their use.\n\n\n\n**Acquiring Visuals**\n\nI\'ve gathered additional visual assets. I\'ve procured both studio headphones for \"Late Night Haze/Focus Flow,\" plus a sprawling city neon image for \"Hyper-Sonic Fusion\". I am prioritizing high-quality visuals to ensure fidelity to the reference. These assets will soon be integrated.\n\n\n**Collecting Design Assets**\n\nI\'ve acquired three more visuals: an ethereal mountain and nebula for \"Deep Work,\" blue/violet geometric shards for \"Rhythm Reset,\" and a wood-textured speaker for \"Analog Warmth.\" These images are high-resolution and fit the aesthetics precisely. I will categorize them with the previous assets to match them with their design use.\n\n\n**Acquiring Album Art**\n\nI\'ve gathered additional visual assets, including cover art. I\'ve procured both a crystalline abstract structure for the \"My Masterpiece\" playlist, plus a violet and emerald splash for \"Neon Horizon.\" I\'ve also found an asset for mini track art. These assets are high-resolution and fit the aesthetics.\n\n\n**Procuring User Avatars**\n\nI\'ve sourced user avatars. I have gathered the required user avatar URLs, and am ready to integrate them into the profile views. I have prepared three distinct avatar URLs for user profiles. I am now ready to proceed, having captured the necessary visual assets.\n\nI\'ve successfully gathered the required assets for user profiles.\n\n\n"
