  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Defining Global States**\n\nI\'m focusing now on establishing the core global states for the application. My aim is to make these accessible to every component. I\'m considering the best architecture to manage playback state effectively. The challenge is creating an elegant and flexible context mechanism. I am also working to ensure that any component can easily read this global state information.\n\n\n**Specifying Initial States**\n\nI\'ve decided to explicitly define the essential states within the root `App` component. These include states for screen navigation (`activeScreen`), the currently playing song (`currentSong`), playback control (`isPlaying`, `progress`, `volume`), search functionality (`searchQuery`), playlist management (`selectedPlaylist`, `playlists`), song liking (`likedSongIds`), audio settings (`isMuted`), the playback queue (`playQueue`), and shuffle/repeat (`isShuffle`). This approach prioritizes direct property passing for simplicity, but I am keeping custom hooks as an alternative.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will create `/src/components/Sidebar.tsx` to build the persistent left navigation sidebar. It provides direct, highly responsive click handlers to toggle between screens (Home, Library, Now Playing full screen, and the Real-time Analytics Dashboard), styled strictly after the brand guide."
