    thinking: "**Achieving Precise Configuration**\n\nI\'m incredibly pleased to report that the linting and TypeScript compilation, utilizing `--noEmit`, executed flawlessly. This success has allowed for the following key advancements: I\'ve updated `metadata.json` to configure the premium application correctly, naming it \"SonicObsidian\". Furthermore, I\'ve populated the typography pairing with Google Fonts.\n\n\n**Defining Core Data Structures**\n\nI\'ve established the foundational data types within `/src/types.ts` for Songs, Playlists, Artists, and active screens. Alongside that, dynamic collections, with accurate lyrics and high-fidelity album art are now defined in `/src/data.ts`.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I have successfully designed and built **SonicObsidian**, a high-fidelity, fully responsive, and accessible dark-themed music streaming platform and real-time audio analytics dashboard using React, Tailwind CSS, and Recharts.\n\nAll files compiled successfully, and code checks confirm a pristine, warning-free build. Here is a summary of the implemented features:\n\n### \360\237\216\250 Visual Identity & Typography\n*   **Aesthetic Theme**: Standardized on a gorgeous, high-contrast, premium dark mode called **Obsidian Noir**, which can be dynamically toggled into a clean, luxurious **Pristine Slate Light Mode** via the sun/moon button in the header.\n*   **Typography Pairings**: Pairings include the distinctive display font **Sora** (for display-md/display-lg titles) and the highly legible **Inter** body font, accented by **JetBrains Mono** for status codes and numerical metrics.\n*   **Layout Structure**: Organized cleanly into a modular file division (preventing file bloat or token cutoff) with dedicated files for `types.ts`, static mock databases `data.ts`, and individual components under `src/components`.\n\n---\n\n### \360\237\223\261 Core Application Screens\n1.  **Screen 1 \342\200\224 Home Dashboard (`HomeView.tsx`)**:\n    *   **Exclusive Mix Banner**: Displays a featured vinyl showcase styled with an animated, floating soundwave visualizer.\n    *   **Recently Played Bento Grid**: Pre-loads responsive song items (\"Neon Echoes\", \"Frequency Fluid\", \"Obsidian Soul\") that trigger instant playback upon clicking.\n    *   **Asymmetric Curated For You Layout**: Highlights a trending playlist card (\"Hyper-Sonic Fusion\") with a contributor user avatar stack alongside a list of mood-oriented playlists.\n2.  **Screen 2 \342\200\224 Your Library (`LibraryView.tsx`)**:\n    *   Includes filter chips to partition content into Playlists, Followed Artists, and Albums.\n    *   Includes a search bar specific to library items.\n    *   **Recently Played Table**: Shows a tabular list of tracked songs including albums, date added, play indicator icons, and option controllers.\n3.  **Screen 3 \342\200\224 Playlist Detail view (`PlaylistDetailView.tsx`)**:\n    *   Models the sleek look of the \"My Masterpiece\" playlist, showing a high-resolution cover image, description, and meta stats (e.g., owner, song count, duration).\n    *   Provides functional play/pause toggles, and track filters.\n4.  **Screen 4 \342\200\224 Fullscreen Now Playing & Lyrics (`NowPlayingView.tsx`)**:\n    *   Offers a full-bleed player experience.\n    *   **Interactive Visualizer**: Hosts an active HTML5 Canvas wave that continuously draws morphing sine-waves and equalizer bars based on playback state.\n    *   **Live Lyrics Synchronizer**: Features a scrollable lyric sheet that continuously shifts focus and emphasizes the current verse based on elapsed track progress.\n    *   **Up Next Queue**: Keeps listeners engaged with upcoming tracks.\n5.  **Screen 5 \342\200\224 Audio Analytics (`AnalyticsView.tsx`)**:\n    *   **Real-time Streaming Telemetry**: Features real-time tickers for live bitrate (kbps FLAC decode ratios), current safe-environment decibels (dB), buffer cache hit rates, and ping delays that fluctuate as the track plays.\n    *   **Data Visualization Components**: Displays a Recharts `AreaChart` mapping weekly listening habits (Hours vs. Average Volume) alongside a Recharts `PieChart` depicting the listener\'s genre breakdown.\n"
