  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyzing Website Structure**\n\nOkay, I\'m examining the current website structure to understand how song additions might work. So far, I\'ve identified `Sidebar.tsx`, `HomeView.tsx`, and `LibraryView.tsx` as key components. The sidebar\'s options, like playlist creation, are also noted.\n\n\n**Expanding Component Inventory**\n\nI\'ve expanded my component inventory to include `PlaylistDetailView.tsx`, `NowPlayingView.tsx`, `AnalyticsView.tsx`, `CreatePlaylistModal.tsx`, `App.tsx`, and `data.ts`. I\'m trying to pinpoint where a song addition feature might exist. It seems the website doesn\'t explicitly support new song additions or uploads, and relies on a hardcoded song list from `data.ts`. So far, I\'ve confirmed that `mockSongs` from `data.ts` acts as the song database. I\'ve also noted that `App.tsx` uses `mockSongs` as an initial value for the `playQueue` state.\n\n\n**Clarifying User Intent**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the user\'s intent. \"How to add a song\" is a question, not a directive. It means providing a straightforward explanation of the current system\'s song management. I am also aware of that I should follow user intent directives. The system uses a static `data.ts` file for song data. It doesn\'t allow for uploads or dynamic additions.\n\n\n**Confirming Static Data Dependency**\n\nI\'ve verified the static nature of the song data. There\'s no explicit upload feature. The UI primarily allows playlist creation (pre-filled) and liking songs, which adds to a \"Liked Tracks\" section. `App.tsx` directly imports and uses `mockSongs` from `./data`, setting the initial `playQueue` state. `LibraryView.tsx` also filters `mockSongs` based on liked songs, confirming its direct dependency on the static data.\n\n\n**Formulating Initial Response**\n\nI\'m solidifying the response. The application uses a hardcoded song list from `data.ts`, meaning no \"Add Song\" form exists. I\'ll outline the current playlist/liking functionality. I\'m also planning to suggest an \"Add Custom Track\" feature with a form. I\'ll explain everything first, and then ask if the user wants this implemented.\n\n\n**Crafting Initial Response**\n\nI\'m now putting the finishing touches on the response. My focus is on providing a clear and respectful explanation of the current song management system. I\'ll explain how songs are preloaded, and how users can interact with them through playlists and liking. Afterwards, I\'ll offer to create a user-friendly form for custom song additions. I\'m aiming for a concise, informative, and friendly tone.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Currently, **SonicObsidian** is configured with a pre-loaded, curated database of high-fidelity tracks (such as *Midnight Reflections* and *Neon Echoes*) defined within the system\'s database configuration (`src/data.ts`). \n\nHere is how you can manage and organize songs with the existing user interface:\n\n### 1. Adding Songs to \"Your Library\"\n* Navigate to **Home** or **Your Library**.\n* Locate any song in the lists.\n* Click the **Heart icon (\342\235\244\357\270\217)** on the song row or in the bottom player bar. \n* This dynamically binds the song to your **Liked Tracks** collection accessible via the Library sidebar tab.\n\n### 2. Crafting Custom Playlists\n* Click the **Create Playlist** button in the left sidebar.\n* Provide a **Name**, a **Description**, and select a **Theme Cover**.\n* Click **Generate Playlist**. This creates a custom playlist container pre-aligned with a high-fidelity starting sequence.\n\n---\n\n### Would you like to add a custom \"Upload / Add Song\" feature?\nSince this is currently a high-fidelity streaming interface, we can easily build an **\"Add New Track\" form/modal** for you! This would let you dynamically input:\n1. **Song Title & Artist Name**\n2. **Album Title & Cover Art URL**\n3. **Song duration & Lyrics segment lines**\n\nOnce submitted, the new track would be seamlessly registered in your library and playable just like the preloaded songs. \n\n**Let me know if you would like me to implement this feature for you!**"
