s very clear.\n\n\n**Defining Storage Strategy**\n\nI\'m now evaluating storage options. It seems like using React state, initialized from `localStorage`, is best for immediate use. This allows persistence within the browser for previewing, and I can then offer clear explanations of `localStorage` versus Firestore. The user\'s goal is to store songs and playlists for now, so I\'ll ask for confirmation before pursuing a database solution. The user wants to understand the where and how.\n\n\n**Implementing Song Feature**\n\nI am now focusing on the \"Add Song\" functionality. My plan is to add a song creation feature, with options for drag-and-drop or selection of audio files (mp3, wav, etc.) and cover images (jpg, png). I\'ll include input fields for title, artist, and genre. I\'ll utilize React and HTML5\'s audio capabilities to handle playback. I\'ll need to figure out how to structure the UI, potentially adding a button or modal in the Sidebar or Library. I am now prioritizing the implementation of the file upload and playback.\n\n\n**Verifying Audio Element**\n\nI\'m now diving into the audio playback implementation. I\'m focusing on creating an object URL using `URL.createObjectURL(file)` to let users listen to uploaded tracks. I will store either an external URL or a blob URL (or Base64 data) inside the `Song` type or state. I need to confirm whether our current player uses an actual `<audio>` tag or a simulated progress timer. I\'m checking `BottomPlayer.tsx` and `App.tsx` for the `<audio>` element. It looks like it simulates progress.\n\n\n**Integrating Audio Playback**\n\nI\'m now implementing real HTML5 audio playback within `App.tsx`! It feels so great to be able to actually play the audio files that are uploaded by users. I will be incorporating the `<audio>` element with object URLs for user-uploaded audio files to ensure seamless playback of real audio. The current setup simulates progress, but by using actual playback, we can support audio uploads by real users. I\'m focusing on making sure any song, mock or real, can play seamlessly. I will make sure this is full-featured and functional.\n\n\n**Adding Playlist Integration**\n\nI\'m now prioritizing the implementation of playlist features. I\'ll add an option within `PlaylistDetailView` (or its creation/editing equivalent) that lets users add songs from the website\'s available library. Also, I\'m making created playlists public, so I will set `isPublic: true` in the state and remove the toggle. Lastly, I\'ll be creating a new analytics view to display playlist-specific statistics, such as track count, duration, and genre breakdown.\n\n\n"
