  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Playlist Analysis**\n\nI\'ve got it! The user wants playlist-specific insights. No more static weekly habits. We need to integrate playlist selection directly into the H-Fi Analytics. This means a way to choose a playlist from within the screen itself. The current design needs to allow this!\n\n\n**Expanding Playlist Integration**\n\nI\'ve got a fantastic solution! I can pass a selected playlist as an initial prop to `AnalyticsView` AND provide a dynamic dropdown within `AnalyticsView` for users to select playlists! This allows real-time analysis updates. I also realized we can compute total track count, duration (for bandwidth), and a real genre breakdown based on the *actual* songs in the playlist, aligning perfectly with authentic data. This is so cool!\n\n\n**Addressing Theme Compatibility**\n\nI\'ve pinpointed the light mode issue! The problem lies with hardcoded `text-white` and similar styles. I found the `light-mode` class in `src/index.css`, confirming theme overrides. We need to replace the absolute color classes. I\'ll focus on replacing `text-white` and other problematic instances to ensure visibility in both light and dark modes, using theme-aware classes or variables.\n\n\n**Isolating Mode Conflicts**\n\nI\'ve got the root cause! The body element uses conditional classes for dark/light mode, but other components hardcode text color. Specifically, `text-white` overrides theme styles, causing visibility issues in light mode. This explains the invisible text! Now I\'ll fix the `text-white` instances in `PlaylistDetailView.tsx` and `AnalyticsView.tsx` to align with the theme.\n\n\n**Optimizing Style Consistency**\n\nI\'ve realized the best solution for theme compatibility. We can use Tailwind\'s `text-obsidian-on-surface` class! It\'s already defined to map to dark gray/black in light mode and off-white in dark mode. This eliminates the need for conditional classes or manual color overrides, ensuring seamless theme adaptation throughout the application.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will view `HomeView.tsx` so we can see how we handle text colors and elements in light mode there, as well as where we remove the initial playlists."
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 8
      nanos: 307361685
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
