    thinking: "**Refining PlaylistView**\n\nI\'ve just given `Sidebar.tsx` a clean bill of health. Now, I\'m pivoting to `PlaylistDetailView.tsx`. The core objective is to integrate a \"play randomly\" feature within the playlist, visualized using a theme-consistent shuffle icon \360\237\224\200. The next step involves adapting it to theme changes.\n\n\n**Addressing Color Accessibility Issues**\n\nI\'ve zeroed in on the color accessibility issues within `PlaylistDetailView.tsx`. The core issue is the hardcoded use of `text-white`, which is a problem, especially in light mode. I\'ve pinpointed and updated several instances, specifically on lines 78, 86, 132, and 184, replacing the hardcoded `text-white` with the appropriate obsidian color utility to ensure text visibility across different themes. I\'m now verifying these changes with a visual test.\n\n\n**Integrating Song Functionality**\n\nI\'m now integrating song management functionality in `PlaylistDetailView.tsx`. Specifically, I\'m adding an \"Add Songs\" section, leveraging a global `songs` array for newly uploaded songs. I\'m expanding the `PlaylistDetailViewProps` with `songs`, `onAddSongToPlaylist`, `onRemoveSongFromPlaylist`, and `onPlayPlaylistRandomly` props to manage this functionality. I\'m also ensuring the table row titles are correctly rendered.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will modify `src/components/PlaylistDetailView.tsx` to:\n1. Handle both dark/light mode visibility issues, changing all hardcoded `text-white` occurrences (such as playlist title, song title, search query text) to theme-adaptive text classes or `text-obsidian-on-surface`.\n2. Add a styled \"Play Randomly\" button with a shuffle symbol \360\237\224\200 matching the branding.\n3. Support adding available songs from the website\'s library to the current playlist. It will display a list of all songs in the library that are not already in this playlist, along with a custom styled \"+ Add to Playlist\" control button.\n4. Add a \"Remove Track\" control button next to liked songs in the table so the user can easily curate their public playlist."
